There's a particularly useful piece in `pogpet/docs/video-episodes-roadmap.md`: it already describes almost exactly the performance compiler we want.

It also reports that the existing Blender jaw-morph path has produced a shareable MP4. That's a substantially better starting point than introducing another video generation model.

### One important incompatibility

Freaktown's current `StageRenderer.ts` expects VRM metadata, whereas our Meshy assets can be ordinary GLBs.

That means a generic Meshy model may load successfully into a normal Three.js viewer but fail in Freaktown's VRM-specific stage.

We need a plain GLB fallback renderer, not an entirely new avatar system.

