## 16. Tests and acceptance criteria

Add unit, integration and end-to-end tests.

Minimum tests:

- Exact GLB-to-performance asset lineage.
- Generic GLB fallback versus VRM playback.
- Audible voice synchronised with rendered movement.
- MP4 opens on desktop and mobile.
- Clip survives reload and retains its permalink.
- Vote cannot be submitted twice for rewards.
- A/B order is recorded correctly.
- Credit ledger cannot be manipulated client-side.
- Anonymous browsing works.
- Signing in preserves comparison continuity appropriately.
- Character links resolve to actual Pogtown profiles.
- Product links reference genuine approved OddHobb bindings.
- Cross-account access is rejected.
- Unlinked users cannot inherit another creator's profile.
- Account linking can be revoked.
- Deleted or moderated clips stop being recommended.
- No private media or secrets are exposed through public manifests.

**P0 definition of done:**

A user opens OddHobb, watches two genuine 3D comedy videos, chooses the funnier one, receives the correct server-side reward progress, clicks a character and lands on its canonical Pogtown page.

That character's profile shows its other performances and correct creator attribution.

The same GLB character remains linked to its original OddHobb product asset.

## 17. Implementation discipline

- Review HEAD and current deployment state before changes.
- Preserve existing OddHobb card, checkout, product and Meshy functionality.
- Do not spend Meshy/API credits without authorisation.
- Build incrementally with passing tests.
- Use existing audio, stage, clip and character contracts.
- Use FFmpeg and verified GLB animation capture before considering new generative video models.
- Keep the first release small enough to demonstrate locally.
- Never fabricate votes, ratings, followers or creator metrics in public-facing pages.
- Don't enable cash-equivalent rewards without the discount/accounting system.
- Maintain a clear implementation status document listing completed work, gaps and production blockers.

**Final instruction:** Implement the narrowest working vertical slice first. Prioritise a finished mesh-to-MP4 performance and a working Funnier-to-Pogtown profile link over elaborate social features. The system must be a real product, not just more scaffolding.

