The important commercial opportunity is that a Pogtown character can become popular before somebody buys anything. Its performances attract followers, Funnier helps us understand the audience, and OddHobb becomes the natural place to buy physical objects featuring that character.

This also feeds back into the Living House project: eventually, a customer who discovers a character through Funnier could buy it a physical home and interact with the same persistent Pog through voice, light and AR.

The shared character identity is the foundation. The MP4 is the distribution unit. Funnier is the discovery engine. OddHobb is the physical commerce layer.